From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdsapi: SPN, RDN, mangled-name and credential helpers (3578)

ntdsapi: SPN, RDN, mangled-name and credential helpers; bind and directory calls fail as with no domain

DsMakeSpnA, DsGetSpnA/W, DsFreeSpnArray, DsCrackSpn/DsCrackSpn2, DsClientMakeSpnForTargetServerA,
DsQuoteRdnValue/DsUnquoteRdnValue, DsGetRdnW, DsIsMangledDn/RdnValue, DsCrackUnquotedMangledRdn,
DsMakePasswordCredentials/DsFreePasswordCredentials and the other Free calls are real. DsBind*
finds no domain (ERROR_NO_SUCH_DOMAIN) or no server, DsUnBind clears the handle, and every call
through a binding handle (DsCrackNames, DsList*, DsReplica*, ...) rejects it. Tests added.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZFS4SPPzeH5d2c1MuzqCS
